1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Dividends still depend on closed spreadsheets, intermediaries, and long settlement windows.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:34,000
DiviStock makes an approved shareholder distribution verifiable, self-service, and auditable on Solana.

3
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:54,000
An issuer takes a snapshot, commits it as a Merkle root, and funds a USDC vault.

4
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Here is one SOLX distribution on Devnet: a 25,000 USDC pool and one million eligible shares.

5
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:40,000
This wallet owns 5,000 SOLX shares, so its allocation is 125 USDC. The proof binds this wallet and amount to the snapshot root.

6
00:01:40,000 --> 00:02:03,000
On claim, the program verifies the proof, transfers USDC from the vault, and creates a claim receipt.

7
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:23,000
The receipt PDA prevents a second claim. DiviStock makes every distribution clear and inspectable.
